1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,680
Meet kinhin.

2
00:00:02,970 --> 00:00:04,820
The mindful CI.

3
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:09,400
Self-hosted runners do one job at a time.

4
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:14,770
Jobs queue up, and whatever one job
leaves behind, the next one inherits.

5
00:00:16,070 --> 00:00:17,990
kinhin fixes that.

6
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:24,070
Every job gets its own fresh VM or container,
deleted when the job is done.

7
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:30,050
Jobs arrive, and kinhin scales to
the queue, within your Mac's limits.

8
00:00:30,170 --> 00:00:33,020
Each job gets its own clean instance.

9
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:38,200
macOS VMs and Linux containers,
side by side.

10
00:00:39,070 --> 00:00:42,090
When one fails, the next still starts clean.

11
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:46,720
Every instance is deleted. Nothing lingers.

12
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,870
One line to install.

13
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:55,120
Then kinhin doctor checks your Mac.

14
00:00:59,020 --> 00:01:05,600
It works with GitHub, GitLab, Gitea and Forgejo,
on Tart, apple container or Docker.

15
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:10,330
One job. One VM. Gone when it's done.

16
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:14,600
kinhin.dev. Free, open source, no telemetry.
